{"name":"French Girly","title":"French Girly","revision":220609,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/French_Girly","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This page describes the French Girly aesthetic from Japan. For other similar aesthetics, see French Girl (Western counterpart), Pink Parisian (Western Tumblr aesthetic), or Parisian Girly (children's depictions)."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This style can be commonly found on Instagram and has been reported on by Japanese fashion magazines as well as online sites aimed at young women. French Girly also centers around the clothing of various indie brands that gained notoriety for creating and catering to this aesthetic, largely by the brand Epine."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Silk, lace"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roses, baby's breath, or other flowers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Desserts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marble staircases"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gold mirrors"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"As the fashion part of the aesthetic is derived from Japanese Girly fashion, it closely follows its typical silhouette while also integrating elements associated with parisian fashion(see pink parisian), such as:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Berets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tweed fabric"},{"kind":"list","text":"Floral lace"},{"kind":"list","text":"Houndstood or plaid patterns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blouses with a large tied neck bow"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gold and pearl accents"},{"kind":"list","text":"Quilted handbags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pumps"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"TV Shows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Emily in Paris"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Populaire"},{"kind":"list","text":"American Girl: Grace Stirs Up Success"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Communities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reddit"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Blogs"},{"kind":"list","text":"La Doll"},{"kind":"list","text":"Myrtireve"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tiara"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Vendors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Apres Jour"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cherie Ange"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cherllita"},{"kind":"list","text":"Désir et Raison"},{"kind":"list","text":"Epine"},{"kind":"list","text":"Evelyn"},{"kind":"list","text":"La Doll."},{"kind":"list","text":"La Florence"},{"kind":"list","text":"Manon Tokyo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Meltie"},{"kind":"list","text":"Michell Macaron"},{"kind":"list","text":"Myrtille"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pium"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shrita"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Youtube Channels"},{"kind":"list","text":"あぽちゃんねる"},{"kind":"list","text":"ふーりー / Risa Furusawa"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Pinterest Boards"},{"kind":"list","text":"French Girly by 1209"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"IVE"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/83/French_girly.png/revision/latest?cb=20230325215655","caption":"French Girly · Visual reference 01","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:French_girly.png","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0392-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a2/French_girly_tote.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240416145105","caption":"French Girly · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:French_girly_tote.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0392-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}